# Task 4.2: Supabase Realtime Subscriptions & WebSocket RLS

**Owner:** Backend Engineer | **Risk:** MEDIUM | **Sprint:** 4

---

## Sub-Tasks

### A. Realtime Channel Setup
- [ ] Enable Supabase Realtime on required tables: `complaints`, `notifications`, `sla_breach_log`
- [ ] Create `src/lib/realtime-subscriptions.ts` with typed subscription factories
- [ ] `subscribeToComplaints(channel, departmentId?)` — metadata columns only, zero PHI
- [ ] `subscribeToNotifications(channel, userId)` — personal notification feed
- [ ] `subscribeToBreaches(channel, hospitalId)` — SLA breach events

### B. WebSocket RLS Enforcement
- [ ] Every WebSocket connection passes the user's JWT in the authorization header
- [ ] Supabase Realtime inherits RLS policies from `auth.jwt()` claims
- [ ] Ward Nurses: receive events ONLY for their `department_id`
- [ ] Quality Coordinators: receive events for their entire `hospital_id`
- [ ] Cross-tenant isolation: Hospital A user receives ZERO events from Hospital B

### C. Instant SLA Breach Hoisting
- [ ] Modify [src/store/useSlaStore.ts](file:///c:/Application%20V4.0/src/store/useSlaStore.ts) — add `hoist(complaintId)` method
- [ ] `hoist()` reorders the DataTable state to push the breached complaint to index 0
- [ ] Wire breach subscription callback → `useSlaStore.hoist()` → React re-render
- [ ] Validate: card moves to top of DataTable WITHOUT page refresh

### D. Dashboard Integration
- [ ] Initialize Realtime channels on `/dashboard` mount
- [ ] Cleanup subscriptions on unmount (prevent memory leaks)
- [ ] Handle reconnection gracefully (Supabase Realtime auto-reconnect)

